"""Multi-turn dialogues about what Lumi sees, where the scene CHANGES between turns (written blind, 2026-10-22,
from docs/14 "What Lumi sees" and docs/WORK_PLAN.md "Big night test" fault 1). Every seeing answer, follow-up
("and now?", "really?", "are you sure?", "look again", "지금은?") and correction must come from a fresh look at the
scene of THAT turn, never from what was said before; a wrong correction ("it's white, not blue" while the camera
still sees blue) is checked against the camera, not agreed with.

DIALOGUES = [{"who", "topic", "lang": "en" | "ko" | "mix", "turns": [turn, ...]}]
turn = {"say", "scene", "route", "expect_action", "must", "must_not", "check"}
- scene: what the cameras see at that moment (every turn carries the full scene):
  {"people": [{"id", "dist_m", "side": "front" | "left" | "right" (as Lumi sees it), "top", "bottom" (colour or None),
  "left_hand", "right_hand" (object or None; the PERSON's own left / right hand), "hands_visible", "raised":
  None | "left" | "right" (the person's own hand)}], "objects": [{"name", "colour", "side", "dist_m"}]}.
  Person "A" is the one talking to Lumi; "B" is someone else.
- route: "seeing" (answered from the cameras), "llm" (talk: thanks, a remark), "end" (goodbye), "act" (a motion).
- expect_action: "none" or the motion asked ("look me").
- must / must_not: case-insensitive regexes on the spoken reply (every must matches, no must_not does). must_not
  names only the stale or wrong claim (written so "not in your left hand any more" does not trip it).
- check: one line on what a right answer does (for a judge).

train: fixes may be made from these.
"""

